--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -12,4 +12,10 @@ Each line of an events file is a JSON object:
 
 Collectors run in several regions and stamp events with their own UTC offset. Legacy collectors (anything installed before 2024) write naive timestamps such as `2024-03-09 22:10:00`; those are UTC. Blank lines are ignored.
 
+To count only recent events, pass `--since` with a date (`YYYY-MM-DD`):
+
+    python -m evlog report events.jsonl --since 2024-03-10
+
+This keeps events at or after midnight UTC on that date. Each timestamp is compared as an absolute instant, so an event stamped `2024-03-09T23:30:00-05:00` (which is 04:30 UTC on the 10th) is included, and naive timestamps are read as UTC. A malformed date is rejected with a usage error.
+
 Run the tests with `python -m unittest`.
